#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:32
msgid "Executor Objects"
msgstr "Objekty Executor"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:36
msgid ""
"An abstract class that provides methods to execute calls asynchronously.  It"
" should not be used directly, but through its concrete subclasses."
msgstr ""
"Abstraktní třída, která poskytuje metody pro asynchronní provádění volání. "
"Neměla by být používána přímo, ale pouze přes její konkrétní podtřídy."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:41
msgid ""
"Schedules the callable, *fn*, to be executed as ``fn(*args, **kwargs)`` and "
"returns a :class:`Future` object representing the execution of the callable."
" ::"
msgstr ""
"Naplánuje spuštění volatelného objektu *fn* jako ``fn(*args, **kwargs)`` a "
"vrací objekt :class:`Future` reprezentující spuštění volatelného objektu. ::"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:45
msgid ""
"with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as executor:\n"
"    future = executor.submit(pow, 323, 1235)\n"
"    print(future.result())"
msgstr ""
"with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as executor:\n"
"    future = executor.submit(pow, 323, 1235)\n"
"    print(future.result())"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:51
msgid "Similar to :func:`map(fn, *iterables) <map>` except:"
msgstr "Podobné jako :func:`map(fn, *iterables) <map>` s výjimkami:"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:53
msgid ""
"The *iterables* are collected immediately rather than lazily, unless a "
"*buffersize* is specified to limit the number of submitted tasks whose "
"results have not yet been yielded. If the buffer is full, iteration over the"
" *iterables* pauses until a result is yielded from the buffer."
msgstr ""
"*iterables* jsou shromáŽěny okamžitě spolu s víle pomalého náčrtání, ledli "
"není specifikován *buffersize* pro omezení počtu odesláných úloh, jejichž "
"výsledky nebyly ještě vydány. Pokud je vyrovnávací paměť plná, iterační "
"proces přes *iterables* se pozastaví, dokud není výsledek vydán z "
"vyrovnávací paměti."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:58
msgid ""
"*fn* is executed asynchronously and several calls to *fn* may be made "
"concurrently."
msgstr ""
"*fn* je spouštěn asynchronně a několik volání *fn* může být prováděno "
"současně."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:61
msgid ""
"The returned iterator raises a :exc:`TimeoutError` if "
":meth:`~iterator.__next__` is called and the result isn't available after "
"*timeout* seconds from the original call to :meth:`Executor.map`. *timeout* "
"can be an int or a float.  If *timeout* is not specified or ``None``, there "
"is no limit to the wait time."
msgstr ""
"Vrácený iterátor vyvolá :exc:`TimeoutError`, je-li volána "
":meth:`~iterator.__next__` a výsledek není k dispozici po *timeout* "
"sekundách od původního volání :meth:`Executor.map`. *timeout* může být int "
"nebo float. Není-li *timeout* specifikován nebo je ``None``, neexistuje "
"žádný limit času čekání."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:67
msgid ""
"If a *fn* call raises an exception, then that exception will be raised when "
"its value is retrieved from the iterator."
msgstr ""
"Je-li volání *fn* vyvolat výjimku, bude tato výj imka vyvolana při získání "
"její hodnoty z iterátoru."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:70
msgid ""
"When using :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor`, this method chops *iterables* into "
"a number of chunks which it submits to the pool as separate tasks.  The "
"(approximate) size of these chunks can be specified by setting *chunksize* "
"to a positive integer.  For very long iterables, using a large value for "
"*chunksize* can significantly improve performance compared to the default "
"size of 1.  With :class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` and "
":class:`InterpreterPoolExecutor`, *chunksize* has no effect."
msgstr ""
"Při použití :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` tato metoda rozdělí *iterables* do "
"několika částí, které odeslabě do fondu jako samostatné úlohy. Přibližnout "
"velikost těchto částí lze zadat nastavením *chunksize* na kladné celé číslo."
" Pro velmi dlouhé iterable lze použití velké hodnoty *chunksize* výrazně "
"zlepšit výkon ve srovnání s výchozí hodnotou 1. S "
":class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` a :class:`InterpreterPoolExecutor` *chunksize* "
"nemá žádný efekt."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:79
msgid "Added the *chunksize* parameter."
msgstr "Přidán parametr *chunksize*."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:82
msgid "Added the *buffersize* parameter."
msgstr "Přidán parametr *buffersize*."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:87
msgid ""
"Signal the executor that it should free any resources that it is using when "
"the currently pending futures are done executing.  Calls to "
":meth:`Executor.submit` and :meth:`Executor.map` made after shutdown will "
"raise :exc:`RuntimeError`."
msgstr ""
"Signalizuje Executor, že by měl osačit jakékoliv zdroje, které používá, když"
" jsou dokončena aktuálně příchodující futures. Volání "
":meth:`Executor.submit` a :meth:`Executor.map` provedena po vypnutí vyvolají"
" :exc:`RuntimeError`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:92
msgid ""
"If *wait* is ``True`` then this method will not return until all the pending"
" futures are done executing and the resources associated with the executor "
"have been freed.  If *wait* is ``False`` then this method will return "
"immediately and the resources associated with the executor will be freed "
"when all pending futures are done executing.  Regardless of the value of "
"*wait*, the entire Python program will not exit until all pending futures "
"are done executing."
msgstr ""
"Je-li *wait* ``True``, tato metoda se nevrátí, dokud nejsou dokončena "
"všechna příchodující futures a zdroje asociované s executor nejsou osačeny. "
"Je-li *wait* ``False``, tato metoda se vrátí okamžitě a zdroje asociované s "
"executor budou osačeny, když budou dokončena všechna příchodující futures. "
"Bez ohledu na hodnotu *wait* se celý program Python neskotčí, dokud nebudou "
"dokončena všechna příchodující futures."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:100
msgid ""
"If *cancel_futures* is ``True``, this method will cancel all pending futures"
" that the executor has not started running. Any futures that are completed "
"or running won't be cancelled, regardless of the value of *cancel_futures*."
msgstr ""
"Je-li *cancel_futures* ``True``, tato metoda zruší všechna příchodující "
"futures, která executor ještě nezatočal spouštět. Jakákoliv futures, která "
"jsou dokončena nebo právě běží, nebudou zrušena, bez ohledu na hodnotu "
"*cancel_futures*."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:105
msgid ""
"If both *cancel_futures* and *wait* are ``True``, all futures that the "
"executor has started running will be completed prior to this method "
"returning. The remaining futures are cancelled."
msgstr ""
"Jsou-li *cancel_futures* i *wait* ``True``, všechna futures, která executor "
"začal spouštět, budou dokončena před návrátem této metody. Zbýjcí futures "
"jsou zrušena."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:109
msgid ""
"You can avoid having to call this method explicitly if you use the executor "
"as a :term:`context manager` via the  :keyword:`with` statement, which will "
"shutdown the :class:`Executor` (waiting as if :meth:`Executor.shutdown` were"
" called with *wait* set to ``True``)::"
msgstr ""
"Její volání můžete vyhnout, pokud executor používate jako :term:`context "
"manager` prostřednictvím :keyword:`with` příkazu, který vypne "
":class:`Executor` (as pokud by byla volána :meth:`Executor.shutdown` s "
"*wait* nastaveným na ``True``)::"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:114
msgid ""
"import shutil\n"
"with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) as e:\n"
"    e.submit(shutil.copy, 'src1.txt', 'dest1.txt')\n"
"    e.submit(shutil.copy, 'src2.txt', 'dest2.txt')\n"
"    e.submit(shutil.copy, 'src3.txt', 'dest3.txt')\n"
"    e.submit(shutil.copy, 'src4.txt', 'dest4.txt')"
msgstr ""
"import shutil\n"
"with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) as e:\n"
"    e.submit(shutil.copy, 'src1.txt', 'dest1.txt')\n"
"    e.submit(shutil.copy, 'src2.txt', 'dest2.txt')\n"
"    e.submit(shutil.copy, 'src3.txt', 'dest3.txt')\n"
"    e.submit(shutil.copy, 'src4.txt', 'dest4.txt')"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:121
msgid "Added *cancel_futures*."
msgstr "Přidán *cancel_futures*."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:126
msgid "ThreadPoolExecutor"
msgstr "ThreadPoolExecutor"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:128
msgid ""
":class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` is an :class:`Executor` subclass that uses a "
"pool of threads to execute calls asynchronously."
msgstr ""
":class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` je podmnnožina :class:`Executor`, která používá "
"fond vláken pro asynchronní provádění volání."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:131
msgid ""
"Deadlocks can occur when the callable associated with a :class:`Future` "
"waits on the results of another :class:`Future`.  For example::"
msgstr ""
"K dead-lockům může dojít, když volatelný objekt asociovaný s :class:`Future`"
" čeká na výsledky dalšího :class:`Future`. Například::"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:134
msgid ""
"import time\n"
"def wait_on_b():\n"
"    time.sleep(5)\n"
"    print(b.result())  # b will never complete because it is waiting on a.\n"
"    return 5\n"
"\n"
"def wait_on_a():\n"
"    time.sleep(5)\n"
"    print(a.result())  # a will never complete because it is waiting on b.\n"
"    return 6\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"executor = ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2)\n"
"a = executor.submit(wait_on_b)\n"
"b = executor.submit(wait_on_a)"
msgstr ""
"import time\n"
"def wait_on_b():\n"
"    time.sleep(5)\n"
"    print(b.result())  # b se nikdy nedokončí, protože čeká na a.\n"
"    return 5\n"
"\n"
"def wait_on_a():\n"
"    time.sleep(5)\n"
"    print(a.result())  # a se nikdy nedokončí, protože čeká na b.\n"
"    return 6\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"executor = ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2)\n"
"a = executor.submit(wait_on_b)\n"
"b = executor.submit(wait_on_a)"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:150
msgid "And::"
msgstr "A::"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:152
msgid ""
"def wait_on_future():\n"
"    f = executor.submit(pow, 5, 2)\n"
"    # This will never complete because there is only one worker thread and\n"
"    # it is executing this function.\n"
"    print(f.result())\n"
"\n"
"executor = ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1)\n"
"executor.submit(wait_on_future)"
msgstr ""
"def wait_on_future():\n"
"    f = executor.submit(pow, 5, 2)\n"
"    # Toto se nikdy nedokončí, protože existuje pouze jedno pracovní vlákno a\n"
"    # právě provádí tuto funkci.\n"
"    print(f.result())\n"
"\n"
"executor = ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1)\n"
"executor.submit(wait_on_future)"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:164
msgid ""
"An :class:`Executor` subclass that uses a pool of at most *max_workers* "
"threads to execute calls asynchronously."
msgstr ""
"Podmnnožina :class:`Executor`, která používá fond nejvíše *max_workers* "
"vláken pro asynchronní provádění volání."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:167
msgid ""
"All threads enqueued to ``ThreadPoolExecutor`` will be joined before the "
"interpreter can exit. Note that the exit handler which does this is executed"
" *before* any exit handlers added using ``atexit``. This means exceptions in"
" the main thread must be caught and handled in order to signal threads to "
"exit gracefully. For this reason, it is recommended that "
"``ThreadPoolExecutor`` not be used for long-running tasks."
msgstr ""
"Všechna vlákna zarazená do ``ThreadPoolExecutor`` budou spojena před tím, "
"než se interpret ukkončí. Poznámka: obsluhující funkce pro výstup, která to "
"provádí, jsou spuštěny *před* jakýmikoliv obsluhovného obsluhujícího funkcí "
"přidané pomocí ``atexit``. To znamená, že výjimky v hlavním vláknu musí být "
"zachyceny a zpracovány, aby se signalizovalo vláknům, aby se vypnula "
"elegantně. Z tohoto důvodu se doporučuje nepoužívat ``ThreadPoolExecutor`` "
"pro dlouhotrvající úlohy."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:174
msgid ""
"*initializer* is an optional callable that is called at the start of each "
"worker thread; *initargs* is a tuple of arguments passed to the initializer."
"  Should *initializer* raise an exception, all currently pending jobs will "
"raise a :exc:`~concurrent.futures.thread.BrokenThreadPool`, as well as any "
"attempt to submit more jobs to the pool."
msgstr ""
"*initializer* je volitelné volatelné, které se volá na začátku každého "
"pracovního vlákna; *initargs* je tuple argumentů prošlých inicializéru. "
"Pokud *initializer* vyvolá výjimku, všechny všechny aktuálně příchodující "
"úlohy vyvolají :exc:`~concurrent.futures.thread.BrokenThreadPool`, stejně "
"jako jakýkoliv pokus o odeslání dalších úloh do fondu."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:180
msgid ""
"If *max_workers* is ``None`` or not given, it will default to the number of "
"processors on the machine, multiplied by ``5``, assuming that "
":class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` is often used to overlap I/O instead of CPU work"
" and the number of workers should be higher than the number of workers for "
":class:`ProcessPoolExecutor`."
msgstr ""
"Je-li *max_workers* ``None`` nebo není uveden, bude nastaven na počet "
"procesorů v počítači vynásoben ``5``, za předpokladu, že "
":class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` je často používán k překrytí I/O místo práce s "
"CPU a počet pracovních prvků by měl být vyšší než počet pracovných prvků pro"
" :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:188
msgid ""
"Added the *thread_name_prefix* parameter to allow users to control the "
":class:`threading.Thread` names for worker threads created by the pool for "
"easier debugging."
msgstr ""
"Přidán parametr *thread_name_prefix*, který umožňuje uživatelům ovládat "
"jména :class:`threading.Thread` pro pracovní vlákna vytvorená fondem pro "
"snadnovou ladění."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:193
#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:403
msgid "Added the *initializer* and *initargs* arguments."
msgstr "Přidány argumenty *initializer* a *initargs*."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:196
msgid ""
"Default value of *max_workers* is changed to ``min(32, os.cpu_count() + "
"4)``. This default value preserves at least 5 workers for I/O bound tasks. "
"It utilizes at most 32 CPU cores for CPU bound tasks which release the GIL. "
"And it avoids using very large resources implicitly on many-core machines."
msgstr ""
"Výchozí hodnota *max_workers* je změněna na ``min(32, os.cpu_count() + 4)``."
" Tato výchozí hodnota zachovává nejméně 5 pracovních prvků pro I/O vlákna. "
"Využívá nejvíše 32 CPU jáder pro úlohy závislé na CPU, které uvoľu GIL. A "
"vyhýba se implicitnímu použití velmi velkých zdrojů na postranních "
"počítačích."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:202
msgid ""
"ThreadPoolExecutor now reuses idle worker threads before starting "
"*max_workers* worker threads too."
msgstr ""
"ThreadPoolExecutor nyní znovupoužívá neatraktivné pracovní vlákna před "
"spuštěním *max_workers* pracovních vláken."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:205
msgid ""
"Default value of *max_workers* is changed to ``min(32, "
"(os.process_cpu_count() or 1) + 4)``."
msgstr ""
"Výchozí hodnota *max_workers* je změněna na ``min(32, "
"(os.process_cpu_count() or 1) + 4)``."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:213
msgid "ThreadPoolExecutor Example"
msgstr "Příklad ThreadPoolExecutor"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:216
#, python-brace-format, python-format
msgid ""
"import concurrent.futures\n"
"import urllib.request\n"
"\n"
"URLS = ['http://www.foxnews.com/',\n"
"        'http://www.cnn.com/',\n"
"        'http://europe.wsj.com/',\n"
"        'http://www.bbc.co.uk/',\n"
"        'http://nonexistent-subdomain.python.org/']\n"
"\n"
"# Retrieve a single page and report the URL and contents\n"
"def load_url(url, timeout):\n"
"    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=timeout) as conn:\n"
"        return conn.read()\n"
"\n"
"# We can use a with statement to ensure threads are cleaned up promptly\n"
"with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=5) as executor:\n"
"    # Start the load operations and mark each future with its URL\n"
"    future_to_url = {executor.submit(load_url, url, 60): url for url in URLS}\n"
"    for future in concurrent.futures.as_completed(future_to_url):\n"
"        url = future_to_url[future]\n"
"        try:\n"
"            data = future.result()\n"
"        except Exception as exc:\n"
"            print('%r generated an exception: %s' % (url, exc))\n"
"        else:\n"
"            print('%r page is %d bytes' % (url, len(data)))"
msgstr ""
"import concurrent.futures\n"
"import urllib.request\n"
"\n"
"URLS = ['http://www.foxnews.com/',\n"
"        'http://www.cnn.com/',\n"
"        'http://europe.wsj.com/',\n"
"        'http://www.bbc.co.uk/',\n"
"        'http://nonexistent-subdomain.python.org/']\n"
"\n"
"# Ziskani jedne stranky a vykladani URL a obsahu\n"
"def load_url(url, timeout):\n"
"    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=timeout) as conn:\n"
"        return conn.read()\n"
"\n"
"# Muzeme pouzit prikaz with, abychom se ujistili, ze vlakna budou cistovana vcas.\n"
"with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=5) as executor:\n"
"    # Zahaji operace nacteni a oznaci kazde future jeho URL\n"
"    future_to_url = {executor.submit(load_url, url, 60): url for url in URLS}\n"
"    for future in concurrent.futures.as_completed(future_to_url):\n"
"        url = future_to_url[future]\n"
"        try:\n"
"            data = future.result()\n"
"        except Exception as exc:\n"
"            print('%r generated an exception: %s' % (url, exc))\n"
"        else:\n"
"            print('%r page is %d bytes' % (url, len(data)))"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:245
msgid "InterpreterPoolExecutor"
msgstr "InterpreterPoolExecutor"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:249
msgid ""
"The :class:`InterpreterPoolExecutor` class uses a pool of interpreters to "
"execute calls asynchronously.  It is a :class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` subclass,"
" which means each worker is running in its own thread. The difference here "
"is that each worker has its own interpreter, and runs each task using that "
"interpreter."
msgstr ""
"Trida :class:`InterpreterPoolExecutor` pouziva fond interpretu pro "
"asynchronni provadeni volani. Je to potomek :class:`ThreadPoolExecutor`, coz"
" znamena, ze kazdy pracovni prvek behi ve svem vlaknu. Rozdil spociva v tom,"
" ze kazdy pracovni prvek ma svuj vlastni interpret a kazde ulohy provadi "
"pomoci tohoto interpretu."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:255
msgid ""
"The biggest benefit to using interpreters instead of only threads is true "
"multi-core parallelism.  Each interpreter has its own :term:`Global "
"Interpreter Lock <global interpreter lock>`, so code running in one "
"interpreter can run on one CPU core, while code in another interpreter runs "
"unblocked on a different core."
msgstr ""
"Nejvetsi vyhodou pouziti interpretu miste jen vlaken je pravda multi-core "
"parallelismus. Kazdy interpret ma svou vlastni :term:`Global Interpreter "
"Lock <global interpreter lock>`, takze kod spusteny v jednom interpreteru "
"muze behet na jednom CPU jadru, zatimco kod v jinem interpreteru behi "
"blokovan na jinem jadru."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:261
msgid ""
"The tradeoff is that writing concurrent code for use with multiple "
"interpreters can take extra effort.  However, this is because it forces you "
"to be deliberate about how and when interpreters interact, and to be "
"explicit about what data is shared between interpreters. This results in "
"several benefits that help balance the extra effort, including true multi-"
"core parallelism,  For example, code written this way can make it easier to "
"reason about concurrency.  Another major benefit is that you don't have to "
"deal with several of the big pain points of using threads, like race "
"conditions."
msgstr ""
"Kompromisem je, ze psani konkurencniho kodu pro pouziti s vice interprety "
"muze vynutit dalsi ucel. To vsak plyne z toho, ze vas nuti byt vedomi toho, "
"jak a kdy se interprety vzajemne interaguji, a byt explicitni o tom, ktera "
"data se mezi interprety sdileji. To ma za nasledek nektere vyhody, ktere "
"pomahaji zvazit dalsi ucel, vcetne skutecneho multi-core paralelismu. "
"Napriklad kod napsany timto zpusobem muze usnadnit uvazovani o soubeznosti. "
"Dalsi hlavni vyhoda je, ze nemusite resit nektere hlavni problemy pouzivani "
"vlaken, jako napriklad zavody o prostredky."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:271
msgid ""
"Each worker's interpreter is isolated from all the other interpreters. "
"\"Isolated\" means each interpreter has its own runtime state and operates "
"completely independently.  For example, if you redirect :data:`sys.stdout` "
"in one interpreter, it will not be automatically redirected to any other "
"interpreter.  If you import a module in one interpreter, it is not "
"automatically imported in any other.  You would need to import the module "
"separately in interpreter where you need it.  In fact, each module imported "
"in an interpreter is a completely separate object from the same module in a "
"different interpreter, including :mod:`sys`, :mod:`builtins`, and even "
"``__main__``."
msgstr ""
"Interpret kazdeho pracovniho prvku je izolovan od vsech ostatnich "
"interpretu. \"Izolace\" znamena, ze kazdy interpret ma svuj vlastni stav "
"behoveho prostredi a operuje zcela nezavisle. Pokud napriklad presmerojete "
":data:`sys.stdout` v jednom interpreteru, nebude to automaticky presmerovno "
"do zadneho jineho interpretu. Pokud importujete modul v jednom interpreteru,"
" automaticky se neimportuje do zadneho jineho. Museli byste modul importovat"
" samostatne v kazdem interpreteru, ktery ho potrebujete. Ve skutecnosti je "
"kazdy modul importovany v interpreteru zcela samostatnym objektem od "
"stejneho modulu v jinem interpreteru, vcetne :mod:`sys`, :mod:`builtins` a "
"dokonce i ``__main__``."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:283
msgid ""
"Isolation means a mutable object, or other data, cannot be used by more than"
" one interpreter at the same time.  That effectively means interpreters "
"cannot actually share such objects or data.  Instead, each interpreter must "
"have its own copy, and you will have to synchronize any changes between the "
"copies manually.  Immutable objects and data, like the builtin singletons, "
"strings, and tuples of immutable objects, don't have these limitations."
msgstr ""
"Izolace znamena, ze meneny objekt nebo jina data nemohou byt pouzivana vice "
"nez jednim interpreteru soucasne. To v efektu znamena, ze interprety nemohou"
" takove objekty nebo data ve skutecnosti sdilet. Miste toho kazdy interpret "
"musi mit vlastni kopii a budete muset synchronizovat zmeny mezi kopiemi "
"rucne. Nemenitelne objekty a data, jako jsou vestavenem jedincky, retezce a "
"tuples nemennych objektu, nemaji tato omezeni."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:291
msgid ""
"Communicating and synchronizing between interpreters is most effectively "
"done using dedicated tools, like those proposed in :pep:`734`.  One less "
"efficient alternative is to serialize with :mod:`pickle` and then send the "
"bytes over a shared :mod:`socket <socket>` or :func:`pipe <os.pipe>`."
msgstr ""
"Komunikace a synchronizace mezi interprety je nejlepe provedena pouzitim "
"venovanych nastroju, jako jsou ty navrhovane v :pep:`734`. Mene ucinnou "
"alternativou je serializace s :mod:`pickle` a pote odeslani bytu pres "
"sdilene :mod:`socket <socket>` nebo :func:`pipe <os.pipe>`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:299
msgid ""
"A :class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` subclass that executes calls asynchronously "
"using a pool of at most *max_workers* threads.  Each thread runs tasks in "
"its own interpreter.  The worker interpreters are isolated from each other, "
"which means each has its own runtime state and that they can't share any "
"mutable objects or other data.  Each interpreter has its own :term:`Global "
"Interpreter Lock <global interpreter lock>`, which means code run with this "
"executor has true multi-core parallelism."
msgstr ""
"Potomek :class:`ThreadPoolExecutor`, ktery provadi volani asynchronne "
"pouzitim fondu nejvice *max_workers* vlaken. Kazde vlakno spusta ulohy ve "
"svem vlastnim interpreteru. Pracovni interprety jsou izovany od sebe "
"navzajem, coz znamena, ze kazdy ma svuj vlastni stav behoveho prostredi a ze"
" nemohou sdilet zadne menitelne objekty nebo jina data. Kazdy interpret ma "
"svuj vlastni :term:`Global Interpreter Lock <global interpreter lock>`, coz "
"znamena, ze kod spusteny s timto executorem ma skutecny multi-core "
"paralelismus."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:307
msgid ""
"The optional *initializer* and *initargs* arguments have the same meaning as"
" for :class:`!ThreadPoolExecutor`: the initializer is run when each worker "
"is created, though in this case it is run in the worker's interpreter.  The "
"executor serializes the *initializer* and *initargs* using :mod:`pickle` "
"when sending them to the worker's interpreter."
msgstr ""
"Volitelne argumenty *initializer* a *initargs* maji stejny vyznam jako pro "
":class:`!ThreadPoolExecutor`: initializer je spusten, kdy se kazdy pracovnik"
" vytvorry, nicmene v tomto pripade je spusten v interpreteru pracovnika. "
"Executor serializuje *initializer* a *initargs* pouzitim :mod:`pickle` pri "
"jejich odeslani do interpreteru pracovnika."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:315
msgid ""
"The executor may replace uncaught exceptions from *initializer* with "
":class:`~concurrent.interpreters.ExecutionFailed`."
msgstr ""
"Executor muze nahradit neuchycene vyjimky z *initializer* s "
":class:`~concurrent.interpreters.ExecutionFailed`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:318
msgid "Other caveats from parent :class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` apply here."
msgstr ""
"Ostatni vyhradk z rodicovske :class:`ThreadPoolExecutor` se zde vztahuji."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:320
msgid ""
":meth:`~Executor.submit` and :meth:`~Executor.map` work like normal, except "
"the worker serializes the callable and arguments using :mod:`pickle` when "
"sending them to its interpreter.  The worker likewise serializes the return "
"value when sending it back."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~Executor.submit` a :meth:`~Executor.map` pracuji normalne, vyjimkou "
"jsou pripady, kdy pracovnik serializuje volatelny objekt a argumenty "
"pouzitim :mod:`pickle` pri jejich odeslani do jeho interpreteru. Pracovnik "
"podobne serializuje navratovou hodnotu pri jejich odeslani zpet."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:325
msgid ""
"When a worker's current task raises an uncaught exception, the worker always"
" tries to preserve the exception as-is.  If that is successful then it also "
"sets the ``__cause__`` to a corresponding "
":class:`~concurrent.interpreters.ExecutionFailed` instance, which contains a"
" summary of the original exception. In the uncommon case that the worker is "
"not able to preserve the original as-is then it directly preserves the "
"corresponding :class:`~concurrent.interpreters.ExecutionFailed` instance "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Kdyby aktualni uloha pracovnika vyvola neuchycenou vyjimku, pracovnik se "
"vzdy pokusa zachovat vyjimku tak, jak je. Je-li to uspesne, pak take nastavi"
" ``__cause__`` na odpovidajici instanci "
":class:`~concurrent.interpreters.ExecutionFailed`, ktera obsahuje soupis "
"puvodni vyjimky. V vyjimecnem pripade, kdy pracovnik neni schopen zachovat "
"originalni tak, jak je, pak primo zachova odpovidajici instanci "
":class:`~concurrent.interpreters.ExecutionFailed`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:337
msgid "ProcessPoolExecutor"
msgstr "ProcessPoolExecutor"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:339
msgid ""
"The :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` class is an :class:`Executor` subclass that"
" uses a pool of processes to execute calls asynchronously. "
":class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` uses the :mod:`multiprocessing` module, which "
"allows it to side-step the :term:`Global Interpreter Lock <global "
"interpreter lock>` but also means that only picklable objects can be "
"executed and returned."
msgstr ""
"Trida :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` je potomek :class:`Executor`, ktery "
"pouziva fond procesu pro asynchronni provadeni volani. "
":class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` pouziva modul :mod:`multiprocessing`, ktery mu "
"umoznuje obejit :term:`Global Interpreter Lock <global interpreter lock>`, "
"ale take znamena, ze pouze objekty pickle mohou byt provedeny a vraceany."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:346
msgid ""
"The ``__main__`` module must be importable by worker subprocesses. This "
"means that :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` will not work in the interactive "
"interpreter."
msgstr ""
"Modul ``__main__`` musi byt importovatelny podprocesu pracovnika. To "
"znamena, ze :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` nefunguje v interaktivnim "
"interpreteru."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:349
msgid ""
"Calling :class:`Executor` or :class:`Future` methods from a callable "
"submitted to a :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` will result in deadlock."
msgstr ""
"Volani :class:`Executor` nebo :class:`Future` metod z volatelneho objektu "
"odesilaneho do :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` vyvola deadlock."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:352
msgid ""
"Note that the restrictions on functions and arguments needing to picklable "
"as per :class:`multiprocessing.Process` apply when using "
":meth:`~Executor.submit` and :meth:`~Executor.map` on a "
":class:`ProcessPoolExecutor`. A function defined in a REPL or a lambda "
"should not be expected to work."
msgstr ""
"Poznamenejte, ze omezeni na funkce a argumenty, ktere se musi dat picklenout"
" podle :class:`multiprocessing.Process`, se vztahuje pri pouziti "
":meth:`~Executor.submit` a :meth:`~Executor.map` na "
":class:`ProcessPoolExecutor`. Funkce definovana v REPL nebo lambda by se "
"nema ocekavat, ze bude fungovat."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:359
msgid ""
"An :class:`Executor` subclass that executes calls asynchronously using a "
"pool of at most *max_workers* processes.  If *max_workers* is ``None`` or "
"not given, it will default to :func:`os.process_cpu_count`. If *max_workers*"
" is less than or equal to ``0``, then a :exc:`ValueError` will be raised. On"
" Windows, *max_workers* must be less than or equal to ``61``. If it is not "
"then :exc:`ValueError` will be raised. If *max_workers* is ``None``, then "
"the default chosen will be at most ``61``, even if more processors are "
"available. *mp_context* can be a :mod:`multiprocessing` context or ``None``."
" It will be used to launch the workers. If *mp_context* is ``None`` or not "
"given, the default :mod:`multiprocessing` context is used. See "
":ref:`multiprocessing-start-methods`."
msgstr ""
"Potomek :class:`Executor`, ktery provadi volani asynchronne pouzitim fondu "
"nejvice *max_workers* procesu. Je-li *max_workers* ``None`` nebo nen uveden,"
" bude nastaven na :func:`os.process_cpu_count`. Je-li *max_workers* mensi "
"nebo roven ``0``, pak bude vyvoljsena :exc:`ValueError`. Na Windows musi byt"
" *max_workers* mensi nebo rovny ``61``. Neni-li tomu tak, bude vyvoljsena "
":exc:`ValueError`. Je-li *max_workers* ``None``, pak vybrany vychozi fond "
"bude nejvice ``61``, i kdyz jsou k dispozici vice procesoru. *mp_context* "
"muze byt kontextem :mod:`multiprocessing` nebo ``None``. Bude pouzit k "
"spusteni pracovniku. Je-li *mp_context* ``None`` nebo nen uveden, pouzije se"
" vychozi kontext :mod:`multiprocessing`. Viz :ref:`multiprocessing-start-"
"methods`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:373
msgid ""
"*initializer* is an optional callable that is called at the start of each "
"worker process; *initargs* is a tuple of arguments passed to the "
"initializer.  Should *initializer* raise an exception, all currently pending"
" jobs will raise a :exc:`~concurrent.futures.process.BrokenProcessPool`, as "
"well as any attempt to submit more jobs to the pool."
msgstr ""
"*initializer* je volititelny volatelny objekt, ktery je volan na zacatku "
"kazdeho procesu pracovnika; *initargs* je tuple argumentu predanidch "
"inicilizeru. Pokud *initializer* vyvola vyjimku, vsechny aktualne cisekajici"
" ulohy vyvolaji :exc:`~concurrent.futures.process.BrokenProcessPool`, stejne"
" jako jakykoli pokus o odeslani dalších uloh do fondu."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:379
msgid ""
"*max_tasks_per_child* is an optional argument that specifies the maximum "
"number of tasks a single process can execute before it will exit and be "
"replaced with a fresh worker process. By default *max_tasks_per_child* is "
"``None`` which means worker processes will live as long as the pool. When a "
"max is specified, the \"spawn\" multiprocessing start method will be used by"
" default in absence of a *mp_context* parameter. This feature is "
"incompatible with the \"fork\" start method."
msgstr ""
"*max_tasks_per_child* je volititelny argument, ktery specifikuje maximalni "
"pocet uloh, ktere muze jeden proces provest pred tim, nez se ukoncí a bude "
"nahrazen cerstym procesem pracovnika. Ve vychozim stavu je "
"*max_tasks_per_child* ``None``, coz znamena, ze procesy pracovnika budou "
"existovat tak dlouho, jak dlouho existuje fond. Je-li zadano maximum, bude "
"ve vychozim stavu pouzita metoda \"spawn\" multiprocessingu v absence "
"parametru *mp_context*. Tato funkce neni kompatibilni s metodou \"fork\"."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:388
msgid ""
"Bugs have been reported when using the *max_tasks_per_child* feature that "
"can result in the :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` hanging in some "
"circumstances. Follow its eventual resolution in :gh:`115634`."
msgstr ""
"Byly hlaseny chyby pri pouziti funkce *max_tasks_per_child*, ktere mohou "
"vest k tomu, ze :class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` se zaseknout v nekterych "
"situacich. Sledujte jeho eventualni vyrieseni v :gh:`115634`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:392
msgid ""
"When one of the worker processes terminates abruptly, a "
":exc:`~concurrent.futures.process.BrokenProcessPool` error is now raised. "
"Previously, behaviour was undefined but operations on the executor or its "
"futures would often freeze or deadlock."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se jeden z procesu pracovnika neocekovane ukonci, je nyn vyvoljsena "
"chyba :exc:`~concurrent.futures.process.BrokenProcessPool`. Predtim chovani "
"bylo nedefinovane, ale operace na executor nebo jeho futures by casto "
"zmrazly nebo zaseknuly se."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:399
msgid ""
"The *mp_context* argument was added to allow users to control the "
"start_method for worker processes created by the pool."
msgstr ""
"Argument *mp_context* byl pridan, aby uzivatelum umoznul ovladat "
"start_method pro procesy pracovnika vytvorene fondem."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:405
msgid ""
"The *max_tasks_per_child* argument was added to allow users to control the "
"lifetime of workers in the pool."
msgstr ""
"Argument *max_tasks_per_child* byl pridan, aby uzivatelum umoznul ovladat "
"zivotnost pracovniku ve fondu."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:409
msgid ""
"On POSIX systems, if your application has multiple threads and the "
":mod:`multiprocessing` context uses the ``\"fork\"`` start method: The "
":func:`os.fork` function called internally to spawn workers may raise a "
":exc:`DeprecationWarning`. Pass a *mp_context* configured to use a different"
" start method. See the :func:`os.fork` documentation for further "
"explanation."
msgstr ""
"Na systemech POSIX, pokud ma vase aplikace vice vlaken a kontext "
":mod:`multiprocessing` pouziva metodu \"fork\" start: Funkce :func:`os.fork`"
" volana interme pro spusteni pracovniku muze vyvolat "
":exc:`DeprecationWarning`. Prejdete *mp_context* konfigurovanym na pouziti "
"jine metody start. Podrobnejsi vysvetleni najdete v dokumentaci "
":func:`os.fork`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:417
msgid ""
"*max_workers* uses :func:`os.process_cpu_count` by default, instead of "
":func:`os.cpu_count`."
msgstr ""
"*max_workers* pouziva :func:`os.process_cpu_count` ve vychozim stavu, miste "
":func:`os.cpu_count`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:421
msgid ""
"The default process start method (see :ref:`multiprocessing-start-methods`) "
"changed away from *fork*. If you require the *fork* start method for "
":class:`ProcessPoolExecutor` you must explicitly pass "
"``mp_context=multiprocessing.get_context(\"fork\")``."
msgstr ""
"Vychozi metoda spusteni procesu (viz :ref:`multiprocessing-start-methods`) "
"se zmenila od *fork*. Pokud potrebujete metodu *fork* start pro "
":class:`ProcessPoolExecutor`, muzite explicitne predat "
"``mp_context=multiprocessing.get_context(\"fork\")``."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:429
msgid ""
"Attempt to terminate all living worker processes immediately by calling "
":meth:`Process.terminate <multiprocessing.Process.terminate>` on each of "
"them. Internally, it will also call :meth:`Executor.shutdown` to ensure that"
" all other resources associated with the executor are freed."
msgstr ""
"Pokuste se neocekovane ukoncit vsechny zijici procesy pracovnika volanem "
":meth:`Process.terminate <multiprocessing.Process.terminate>` na kazdy z "
"nich. Vnitrne se take vola :meth:`Executor.shutdown`, aby se zajistilo, ze "
"vsechny ostatni zdroje spojene s executor jsou освobozeny."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:434
#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:446
msgid ""
"After calling this method the caller should no longer submit tasks to the "
"executor."
msgstr ""
"Po volan se teto metody by volajici nemeli dal podavat ulohy executor."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:441
msgid ""
"Attempt to kill all living worker processes immediately by calling "
":meth:`Process.kill <multiprocessing.Process.kill>` on each of them. "
"Internally, it will also call :meth:`Executor.shutdown` to ensure that all "
"other resources associated with the executor are freed."
msgstr ""
"Pokuste se okamzite zabiti vsechny zijici procesy pracovnika volanem "
":meth:`Process.kill <multiprocessing.Process.kill>` na kazdy z nich. Vnitrne"
" se take vola :meth:`Executor.shutdown`, aby se zajistilo, ze vsechny "
"ostatni zdroje spojene s executor jsou oswobozeny."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:454
msgid "ProcessPoolExecutor Example"
msgstr "Priklad ProcessPoolExecutor"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:457
#, python-format
msgid ""
"import concurrent.futures\n"
"import math\n"
"\n"
"PRIMES = [\n"
"    112272535095293,\n"
"    112582705942171,\n"
"    112272535095293,\n"
"    115280095190773,\n"
"    115797848077099,\n"
"    1099726899285419]\n"
"\n"
"def is_prime(n):\n"
"    if n < 2:\n"
"        return False\n"
"    if n == 2:\n"
"        return True\n"
"    if n % 2 == 0:\n"
"        return False\n"
"\n"
"    sqrt_n = int(math.floor(math.sqrt(n)))\n"
"    for i in range(3, sqrt_n + 1, 2):\n"
"        if n % i == 0:\n"
"            return False\n"
"    return True\n"
"\n"
"def main():\n"
"    with concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor() as executor:\n"
"        for number, prime in zip(PRIMES, executor.map(is_prime, PRIMES)):\n"
"            print('%d is prime: %s' % (number, prime))\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"
msgstr ""
"import concurrent.futures\n"
"import math\n"
"\n"
"PRIMES = [\n"
"    112272535095293,\n"
"    112582705942171,\n"
"    112272535095293,\n"
"    115280095190773,\n"
"    115797848077099,\n"
"    1099726899285419]\n"
"\n"
"def is_prime(n):\n"
"    if n < 2:\n"
"        return False\n"
"    if n == 2:\n"
"        return True\n"
"    if n % 2 == 0:\n"
"        return False\n"
"\n"
"    sqrt_n = int(math.floor(math.sqrt(n)))\n"
"    for i in range(3, sqrt_n + 1, 2):\n"
"        if n % i == 0:\n"
"            return False\n"
"    return True\n"
"\n"
"def main():\n"
"    with concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor() as executor:\n"
"        for number, prime in zip(PRIMES, executor.map(is_prime, PRIMES)):\n"
"            print('%d is prime: %s' % (number, prime))\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:492
msgid "Future Objects"
msgstr "Objekty Future"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:494
msgid ""
"The :class:`Future` class encapsulates the asynchronous execution of a "
"callable. :class:`Future` instances are created by :meth:`Executor.submit`."
msgstr ""
"Trida :class:`Future` zapouzdruje asynchronni vykonavani volatelneho "
"objektu. Instance :class:`Future` jsou vytvoreny :meth:`Executor.submit`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:499
msgid ""
"Encapsulates the asynchronous execution of a callable.  :class:`Future` "
"instances are created by :meth:`Executor.submit` and should not be created "
"directly except for testing."
msgstr ""
"Zapouzdruje asynchronni vykonavani volatelneho objektu. Instance "
":class:`Future` jsou vytvoreny :meth:`Executor.submit` a nemely by byt "
"vytvoreny primo vyjimkou pri testovani."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:505
msgid ""
"Attempt to cancel the call.  If the call is currently being executed or "
"finished running and cannot be cancelled then the method will return "
"``False``, otherwise the call will be cancelled and the method will return "
"``True``."
msgstr ""
"Pokuste se zrusit volani. Je-li volani aktualne provadeno nebo skonceno a "
"nelze ho zrusit, metoda vrati ``False``, jinak bude volani zruseno a metoda "
"vrati ``True``."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:512
msgid "Return ``True`` if the call was successfully cancelled."
msgstr "Vrati ``True``, je-li volani uspesne zruseno."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:516
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the call is currently being executed and cannot be "
"cancelled."
msgstr "Vrati ``True``, je-li volani aktualne provadeno a nelze ho zrusit."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:521
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the call was successfully cancelled or finished running."
msgstr "Vrati ``True``, bylo-li volani uspesne zruseno nebo bylo dokonceno."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:526
msgid ""
"Return the value returned by the call. If the call hasn't yet completed then"
" this method will wait up to *timeout* seconds.  If the call hasn't "
"completed in *timeout* seconds, then a :exc:`TimeoutError` will be raised. "
"*timeout* can be an int or float.  If *timeout* is not specified or "
"``None``, there is no limit to the wait time."
msgstr ""
"Vrati hodnotu vracennou volanim. Pokud volani jeste neskoncilo, metoda cekat"
" az *timeout* sekund. Pokud volani neskoncilo v *timeout* sekundach, bude "
"vyvoljsena :exc:`TimeoutError`. *timeout* muze byt int nebo float. Neni-li "
"*timeout* specifikován nebo je ``None``, neni limit casu cekani."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:533
#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:547
msgid ""
"If the future is cancelled before completing then :exc:`.CancelledError` "
"will be raised."
msgstr ""
"Bylo-li future zruseno pred dokoncenim, bude vyvoljsena "
":exc:`.CancelledError`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:536
msgid ""
"If the call raised an exception, this method will raise the same exception."
msgstr "Pokud volani vyvola vyjimku, metoda vyvoli tutez vyjimku."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:540
msgid ""
"Return the exception raised by the call.  If the call hasn't yet completed "
"then this method will wait up to *timeout* seconds.  If the call hasn't "
"completed in *timeout* seconds, then a :exc:`TimeoutError` will be raised.  "
"*timeout* can be an int or float.  If *timeout* is not specified or "
"``None``, there is no limit to the wait time."
msgstr ""
"Vrati vyjimku vyvolenou volanim. Pokud volani jeste neskoncilo, metoda cekat"
" az *timeout* sekund. Pokud volani neskoncilo v *timeout* sekundach, bude "
"vyvoljsena :exc:`TimeoutError`. *timeout* muze byt int nebo float. Neni-li "
"*timeout* specifikován nebo je ``None``, neni limit casu cekani."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:550
msgid "If the call completed without raising, ``None`` is returned."
msgstr "Pokud volani skoncilo bez vyvolení, je vraceno ``None``."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:554
msgid ""
"Attaches the callable *fn* to the future.  *fn* will be called, with the "
"future as its only argument, when the future is cancelled or finishes "
"running."
msgstr ""
"Pripoji volatilny objekt *fn* k future. *fn* bude volana, s future jako "
"jedinnym argumentem, kdyz je future zruseno nebo skoncilo behy."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:558
msgid ""
"Added callables are called in the order that they were added and are always "
"called in a thread belonging to the process that added them.  If the "
"callable raises an :exc:`Exception` subclass, it will be logged and ignored."
"  If the callable raises a :exc:`BaseException` subclass, the behavior is "
"undefined."
msgstr ""
"Pridane volatilne objekty jsou volany v poradi, v nemz byly pridany a jsou "
"vzdy volany ve vlaknu patrici procesu, ktery je pridal. Pokud volatilny "
"objekt vyvola podtriidu :exc:`Exception`, bude protokolovano a ignorovano. "
"Pokud volatilny objekt vyvola podtriidu :exc:`BaseException`, chovan se je "
"nedefinovane."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:564
msgid ""
"If the future has already completed or been cancelled, *fn* will be called "
"immediately."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se future jiz skoncilo nebo bylo zruseno, *fn* bude volan okamzite."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:567
msgid ""
"The following :class:`Future` methods are meant for use in unit tests and "
":class:`Executor` implementations."
msgstr ""
"Nasledujici metody :class:`Future` jsou urceny pro pouziti v jednotkových "
"testech a implementacich :class:`Executor`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:572
msgid ""
"This method should only be called by :class:`Executor` implementations "
"before executing the work associated with the :class:`Future` and by unit "
"tests."
msgstr ""
"Tato metoda by mela byt volana pouze implementacemi :class:`Executor` pred "
"vykonanim prace spojene s :class:`Future` a jednotkovymi testy."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:576
msgid ""
"If the method returns ``False`` then the :class:`Future` was cancelled, i.e."
" :meth:`Future.cancel` was called and returned ``True``.  Any threads "
"waiting on the :class:`Future` completing (i.e. through :func:`as_completed`"
" or :func:`wait`) will be woken up."
msgstr ""
"Pokud metoda vrati ``False``, pak :class:`Future` bylo zruseno, tzn. "
":meth:`Future.cancel` byla volana a vratila ``True``. Jakekoli vlakna "
"cekajici na dokonceni :class:`Future` (tzn. pres :func:`as_completed` nebo "
":func:`wait`) budou probuzena."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:581
msgid ""
"If the method returns ``True`` then the :class:`Future` was not cancelled "
"and has been put in the running state, i.e. calls to :meth:`Future.running` "
"will return ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Pokud metoda vrati ``True``, pak :class:`Future` nebobl zruseno a bylo "
"umisteno do stavu spusteni, tzn. volani :meth:`Future.running` vratis "
"``True``."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:585
msgid ""
"This method can only be called once and cannot be called after "
":meth:`Future.set_result` or :meth:`Future.set_exception` have been called."
msgstr ""
"Tato metoda muze byt volana pouze jednou a neni mozne ji volat po tom, co "
"byla volana :meth:`Future.set_result` nebo :meth:`Future.set_exception`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:591
msgid ""
"Sets the result of the work associated with the :class:`Future` to *result*."
msgstr "Nastavi vysledek prace spojene s :class:`Future` na *result*."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:594
#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:607
msgid ""
"This method should only be used by :class:`Executor` implementations and "
"unit tests."
msgstr ""
"Tato metoda by mela byt pouzita pouze implementacemi :class:`Executor` a "
"jednotkovymi testy."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:597
#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:610
msgid ""
"This method raises :exc:`concurrent.futures.InvalidStateError` if the "
":class:`Future` is already done."
msgstr ""
"Tato metoda vyvoli :exc:`concurrent.futures.InvalidStateError`, pokud je "
":class:`Future` jiz dokonceno."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:604
msgid ""
"Sets the result of the work associated with the :class:`Future` to the "
":class:`Exception` *exception*."
msgstr ""
"Nastavi vysledek prace spojene s :class:`Future` na :class:`Exception` "
"*exception*."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:616
msgid "Module Functions"
msgstr "Funkce modulu"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:620
msgid ""
"Wait for the :class:`Future` instances (possibly created by different "
":class:`Executor` instances) given by *fs* to complete. Duplicate futures "
"given to *fs* are removed and will be returned only once. Returns a named "
"2-tuple of sets.  The first set, named ``done``, contains the futures that "
"completed (finished or cancelled futures) before the wait completed.  The "
"second set, named ``not_done``, contains the futures that did not complete "
"(pending or running futures)."
msgstr ""
"Cekat na :class:`Future` instance (mozna vytvorene ruznymi instancemi "
":class:`Executor`) dane *fs* aby se dokoncili. Duplikatni futures dane *fs* "
"jsou odstraneny a budou vraceny pouze jednou. Vraci pojmenovanou 2-tuple "
"sady. Prvni sada, pojmenovana ``done``, obsahuje futures, ktera byla "
"dokoncena (skoncena nebo zrusena futures) pred tim, nez se cekani skoncilo. "
"Druha sada, pojmenovana ``not_done``, obsahuje futures, ktera neskoncila "
"(cekajici nebo bezici futures)."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:628
msgid ""
"*timeout* can be used to control the maximum number of seconds to wait "
"before returning.  *timeout* can be an int or float.  If *timeout* is not "
"specified or ``None``, there is no limit to the wait time."
msgstr ""
"*timeout* muze byt pouzit k ovladani maximalniho poctu sekund k cekani pred "
"vracenim. *timeout* muze byt int nebo float. Neni-li *timeout* specifikován "
"nebo je ``None``, neni limit casu cekani."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:632
msgid ""
"*return_when* indicates when this function should return.  It must be one of"
" the following constants:"
msgstr ""
"*return_when* indicuje, kdy by tato funkce mela vratit. Musi to byt jedna z "
"nasledujicich konstant:"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:638
msgid "Constant"
msgstr "Konstanta"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:639
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Popis"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:642
msgid "The function will return when any future finishes or is cancelled."
msgstr "Funkce se vrati, kdyz se jakekoli future skoncilo nebo bylo zruseno."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:645
msgid ""
"The function will return when any future finishes by raising an exception. "
"If no future raises an exception then it is equivalent to "
":const:`ALL_COMPLETED`."
msgstr ""
"Funkce se vrati, kdyz se jakekoli future skoncilo vyvolením vyjimky. Pokud "
"se ziadne future nevyvoli vyjimku, je to ekvivalentni "
":const:`ALL_COMPLETED`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:650
msgid "The function will return when all futures finish or are cancelled."
msgstr "Funkce se vrati, kdyz se vsechna futures skoncila nebo byla zrusena."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:654
msgid ""
"Returns an iterator over the :class:`Future` instances (possibly created by "
"different :class:`Executor` instances) given by *fs* that yields futures as "
"they complete (finished or cancelled futures). Any futures given by *fs* "
"that are duplicated will be returned once. Any futures that completed before"
" :func:`as_completed` is called will be yielded first.  The returned "
"iterator raises a :exc:`TimeoutError` if :meth:`~iterator.__next__` is "
"called and the result isn't available after *timeout* seconds from the "
"original call to :func:`as_completed`.  *timeout* can be an int or float. If"
" *timeout* is not specified or ``None``, there is no limit to the wait time."
msgstr ""
"Vraci iterator pres :class:`Future` instance (mozna vytvorene ruznymi "
"instancemi :class:`Executor`) dane *fs*, ktery zna futures tak, jak se "
"dokoncuji (skoncena nebo zrusena futures). Jakakoli futures dana *fs*, ktere"
" jsou duplikatni, budou vrateny jednou. Jakakoli futures, ktere se skoncila "
"pred volanim :func:`as_completed`, budou vyzvednuty prvni. Vraceny iterator "
"vyvoli :exc:`TimeoutError`, pokud je volana :meth:`~iterator.__next__` a "
"vysledek neni dostupny po *timeout* sekundach od puvodniho volani "
":func:`as_completed`. *timeout* muze byt int nebo float. Neni-li *timeout* "
"specifikován nebo je ``None``, neni limit casu cekani."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:667
msgid ":pep:`3148` -- futures - execute computations asynchronously"
msgstr ":pep:`3148` -- futures - provadeni vypoctu asynchronne"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:668
msgid ""
"The proposal which described this feature for inclusion in the Python "
"standard library."
msgstr ""
"Navrh, ktery popsoval tuto funkcnost pro zarazeni v knihovne standardu "
"Python."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:673
msgid "Exception classes"
msgstr "Tridy vyjimek"

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:679
msgid "Raised when a future is cancelled."
msgstr "Vyvoljsena, pokud je future zruseno."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:683
msgid ""
"A deprecated alias of :exc:`TimeoutError`, raised when a future operation "
"exceeds the given timeout."
msgstr ""
"Zastaraleje alias :exc:`TimeoutError`, vyvoljsena, kdyz operace future "
"prekroci danou timeout."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:688
msgid "This class was made an alias of :exc:`TimeoutError`."
msgstr "Tato trida byla ucinena aliasem :exc:`TimeoutError`."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:693
msgid ""
"Derived from :exc:`RuntimeError`, this exception class is raised when an "
"executor is broken for some reason, and cannot be used to submit or execute "
"new tasks."
msgstr ""
"Odvozeno z :exc:`RuntimeError`, tato trida vyjimek je vyvoljsena, kdyz je "
"executor rozbitny z nejakych duvodu a nelze ji pouzit pro odesilani nebo "
"provedeni novych uloh."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:701
msgid ""
"Raised when an operation is performed on a future that is not allowed in the"
" current state."
msgstr ""
"Vyvoljsena, kdyz je operace provedena na future, ktera neni povolena v "
"aktualni stavu."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:710
msgid ""
"Derived from :exc:`~concurrent.futures.BrokenExecutor`, this exception class"
" is raised when one of the workers of a "
":class:`~concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor` has failed initializing."
msgstr ""
"Odvozeno z :exc:`~concurrent.futures.BrokenExecutor`, tato trida vyjimek je "
"vyvoljsena, kdyz jeden z pracovniku "
":class:`~concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor` se selhalo pri inicializaci."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:721
msgid ""
"Derived from :exc:`~concurrent.futures.thread.BrokenThreadPool`, this "
"exception class is raised when one of the workers of a "
":class:`~concurrent.futures.InterpreterPoolExecutor` has failed "
"initializing."
msgstr ""
"Odvozeno z :exc:`~concurrent.futures.thread.BrokenThreadPool`, tato trida "
"vyjimek je vyvoljsena, kdyz jeden z pracovniku "
":class:`~concurrent.futures.InterpreterPoolExecutor` se selhalo pri "
"inicializaci."

#: ../../library/concurrent.futures.rst:732
msgid ""
"Derived from :exc:`~concurrent.futures.BrokenExecutor` (formerly "
":exc:`RuntimeError`), this exception class is raised when one of the workers"
" of a :class:`~concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor` has terminated in a "
"non-clean fashion (for example, if it was killed from the outside)."
msgstr ""
"Odvozeno z :exc:`~concurrent.futures.BrokenExecutor` (drivejsi "
":exc:`RuntimeError`), tato trida vyjimek je vyvoljsena, kdyz jeden z "
"pracovniku :class:`~concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor` skoncil necliste"
" (napriklad, pokud byl zabit zvence)."
